Chapter: ActiveSkillsTaste
  cites Uoaix chapter ActiveSkillsHiding

 ServUO Scripts/Skills/TasteID.cs, GPL-2.0; ports/ServUO-LICENSE.txt. Taste Identification (36) targets within 2 tiles.
 Food (an item whose economy lot is a food, ep-food) rolls 36 at an even chance per skill point: success finds nothing
 unusual, as no food here carries poison, and failure discerns nothing. A potion (bottle art 0x0F06 to 0x0F0E) is
 already known and named without a roll. A mobile is inappropriate; anything else cannot be tasted.
  as-taste-potion : Integer -> Boolean
  as-taste-potion (graphic) = graphic >= #0F06 & graphic <= #0F0E
  as-taste-food : ActiveSkills, Integer -> Boolean
  as-taste-food (s) (serial) = let at = gv-lot s.vendor serial 0 in at >= 0 & ep-food (list-at s.vendor.lots at).item
  as-taste : AsServices, ActiveSkills, AsActor, WorldObject, WorldObject -> GameReply
  as-taste (services) (s) (a) (player) (obj) =
    if obj.kind == 1 then gs-reply [as-say "You feel that such an action would be inappropriate."] "skills:taste-mobile"
    else if not (if obj.container == 0 then as-near player obj 2 else gv-owned s.items.world obj.serial player.serial 65) then gs-reply [as-say "You are too far away to taste that."] "skills:taste-far"
    else if as-taste-potion obj.graphic then gs-reply [as-say "You already know what kind of potion that is.", as-say (services.item-name obj.serial)] "skills:taste-potion"
    else if not (as-taste-food s obj.serial) then gs-reply [as-say "That's not something you can taste."] "skills:taste-none"
    else if as-roll s a 36 (skc-random a.skills 1000) then gs-reply [as-say "You detect nothing unusual about this substance."] "skills:taste-food"
    else gs-reply [as-say "You cannot discern anything about this substance."] "skills:taste-failed"

